{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789491006,"nonce":"f+Wsy73654R7jwi+ds4kxCuV+RE=","title":"The release analysis classifies every instruction against every name of a site","message":"`analyze_site` walked every instruction of the function for each allocation site, and for each instruction classified it against every derived name of the site (the pointer, its casts, the fields loaded from it): with 49 sites in bench_pipeline's main and a few names each, tens of thousands of classifications, nearly all of them of instructions naming none of them. Now one walk of the instruction's operands settles that first, and only an instruction naming one of the values is classified. `ZYNTAX_REGALLOC=single_pass` also arrives as a measuring switch for Cranelift's quick allocator (it compiles about 40% faster and runs the kernels up to 70% slower; `backtracking` stays).\n\nMeasurements to follow once the machine is quiet: the pass took 6.7 ms on bench_pipeline (main 2.05 ms of analysis, 1.37 ms of phi releases) before.","files":null}]}